  MF2:  Resolved resonance range  (RRR)                           2928 1451   72
       The RRR was generated with TARES-1.43, compiled on         2928 1451   73
       Nov 12 2021, 12:47:37 at Villigen   , Switzerland. The RRR 2928 1451   74
       expands from 0 to 1.499903E+2 eV. A total of               2928 1451   75
       3 l-values are used and 10 resonances. The resonance       2928 1451   76
       formalism is multi-level Breit Wigner (MLBW).              2928 1451   77
       The TARES database for the measured resonances is          2928 1451   78
        ->  default up to 158.928 eV.                             2928 1451   79
       Above this energy, the ladder approach is used.            2928 1451   80
       The ladder approach from the CALENDF code is used to       2928 1451   81
       generate statistical resonances in the unresolved          2928 1451   82
       resonance range. Therefore, the URR is translated into     2928 1451   83
       resolved resonance range. Explanations about the method    2928 1451   84
       can be found in the CALENDF manual: CEA-Report CEA-R-6277  2928 1451   85
       "CALENDF-2010: User manual" by J.C. Sublet, P. Ribon and   2928 1451   86
       M. Coste-Delcaux.                                          2928 1451   87
       The method of creating statistical resonances in the       2928 1451   88
       URR region is described in: "From average parameters to    2928 1451   89
       statistical resolved resonances", D. Rochman et al.,       2928 1451   90
       Annals of Nucl. Ene. 51 (2013) 60.                         2928 1451   91
       The s-wave average level spacing is 158.928 eV and         2928 1451   92
       the s-wave neutron strength is 0.000268571 1e-4.           2928 1451   93
                                                                  2928 1451   94
