***************************** T A L Y S **************************2928 1451  166
                                                                  2928 1451  167
TALYS is a computer code system for the prediction and analysis   2928 1451  168
of nuclear reactions. TALYS simulates reactions that involve      2928 1451  169
neutrons, gamma-rays, protons, deuterons, tritons, helions and    2928 1451  170
alpha-particles, in the 1 keV - 200 MeV energy range. This is     2928 1451  171
achieved by implementing a suite of nuclear reaction models into  2928 1451  172
a single code system. This nuclear data file is based on a        2928 1451  173
theoretical analysis that utilizes the optical model, compound    2928 1451  174
nucleus statistical theory, fission, direct reactions and         2928 1451  175
pre-equilibrium processes, in combination with databases and      2928 1451  176
models for nuclear structure. The following output of TALYS is    2928 1451  177
stored in this data file:                                         2928 1451  178
                                                                  2928 1451  179
- Total, elastic and non-elastic cross sections                   2928 1451  180
- Inelastic cross sections to discrete states                     2928 1451  181
- Exclusive channel cross sections, e.g. (n,g), (n,2n), (n,np),.. 2928 1451  182
- Inelastic scattering angular distributions to discrete states   2928 1451  183
- Exclusive channel energy spectra                                2928 1451  184
- Exclusive channel double-differential spectra                   2928 1451  185
- Exclusive gamma production for discrete states and continuum    2928 1451  186
- Elastic scattering angular distributions                        2928 1451  187
- Recoil data                                                     2928 1451  188
- Total particle cross sections, e.g. (n,xn), (n,xp),..           2928 1451  189
- Total particle energy spectra                                   2928 1451  190
- Total particle double-differential spectra                      2928 1451  191
- Isomeric and ground state cross sections                        2928 1451  192
- Residual production cross sections                              2928 1451  193
                                                                  2928 1451  194
For a description of the used nuclear models and their            2928 1451  195
parameterization we refer to [kon19]. If for this specific        2928 1451  196
nuclide we deviate from the global parameterization, it is made   2928 1451  197
explicit above under Nuclide Specific Information.                2928 1451  198
                                                                  2928 1451  199
